BT /F1 11 Tf 54 594 Td (\223To-morrow fortnight.\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 571.5 Td (\223Ay, so it is,\224 cried her mother, \223and Mrs. Long does not come) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 556.5 Td (back till the day before; so, it will be impossible for her to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 541.5 Td (introduce him, for she will not know him herself.\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 519 Td (\223Then, my dear, you may have the advantage of your friend, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 504 Td (introduce Mr. Bingley to her.\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 481.5 Td (\223Impossible, Mr. Bennet, impossible, when I am not acquainted with) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 466.5 Td (him myself; how can you be so teasing?\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 444 Td (\223I honour your circumspection. A fortnight\222s acquaintance is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 429 Td (certainly very little. One cannot know what a man really is by the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 414 Td (end of a fortnight. But if we do not venture, somebody else will;) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 399 Td (and after all, Mrs. Long and her nieces must stand their chance;) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 384 Td (and, therefore, as she will think it an act of kindness, if you) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 369 Td (decline the office, I will take it on myself.\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 346.5 Td (The girls stared at their father. Mrs. Bennet said only,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 331.5 Td (\223Nonsense, nonsense!\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 309 Td (\223What can be the meaning of that emphatic exclamation?\224 cried he.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 294 Td (\223Do you consider the forms of introduction, and the stress that is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 279 Td (laid on them, as nonsense? I cannot quite agree with you there.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 264 Td (What say you, Mary? For you are a young lady of deep reflection, I) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 249 Td (know, and read great books, and make extracts.\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 226.5 Td (Mary wished to say something very sensible, but knew not how.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 204 Td (\223While Mary is adjusting her ideas,\224 he continued, \223let us return) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 189 Td (to Mr. Bingley.\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 166.5 Td (\223I am sick of Mr. Bingley,\224 cried his wife.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 144 Td (\223I am sorry to hear that; but why did you not tell me so before?) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 129 Td (If I had known as much this morning, I certainly would not have) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 114 Td (called on him. It is very unlucky; but as I have actually paid the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 99 Td (visit, we cannot escape the acquaintance now.\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54 76.5 Td (The astonishment of the ladies was just what he wished--that of) Tj ET
endstream
